    "type": "question",
    "label": "35",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$\\frac{2x}{x-3}-\\frac{x+1}{x+2}=1.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-\\frac97$.",
      "worked": "$x\\ne3,-2$. Multiply by $(x-3)(x+2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x(x+2)-(x+1)(x-3)&=(x-3)(x+2)\\\\x^2+6x+3&=x^2-x-6\\\\7x+9&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac97.\\end{align*}$$\nThis value is admissible.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
